## Objective
Record, as one release, the feature work that shipped between v0.2.0 and the
2026-09-26 roadmap reconcile without a card of its own: six GitHub epics that
closed schema-backed gaps, plus the first measured performance work from #51.
Written after the fact — this card is history, not a plan.

## Goals (all shipped)
- Epic #87 (PR #94) — master text styles, theme style lists, `SlideMaster.apply_theme`.
- Epic #79 (PR #96) — freeform curves/arcs, line cap/join, picture fill, non-linear
  gradients, table row/column add/remove, cell text direction, autofit readouts.
- Epic #56 (PR #99) — notes size, custom shows, slide-show settings, table-style listing,
  embedded fonts; `LazyXmlPart` keeps untouched parts byte-stable.
- Epic #62 (PR #101) — SmartArt detection, node-tree read, node text edit.
- Epic #66 (PR #103) — chartex charts (read all types; add waterfall, histogram, box &
  whisker, treemap, sunburst, funnel) and the classic-chart data table.
- Epic #75 (PR #105) — `add_audio`, movie/audio trim and fade, 3D models / zooms /
  equations listed as read-only `AlternateContentShape`s.
- Issue #51 (PRs #107–#109) — cached `qn()` and compiled XPath (~39% faster per deck),
  `examples/batch_process.py`, and the `tests/perf/` harness.
- Fix: `PP_MEDIA_TYPE.SOUND` is 2 (was an alias of `OTHER`).

## Dependencies
- `v0.2.0` — the feature manifest and gap log these epics were planned against.

## Out of scope
- Everything the planned cards own: real-world corpus (v0.4.0), transitions/animations
  and custom layouts (v0.5.0), the rest of the performance pass (v0.6.0), cross-run text
  (v0.7.0), example scripts and docstrings (v0.3.1, v0.3.2).

## Objectives / acceptance
- Each epic's sub-issues closed by their PR; `pytest -q` green at each merge (3657 tests
  at the last one).
- Package version `0.3.0` in `pyproject.toml` and `pptx.__version__`.
- Human-gated PowerPoint checks for these features are tracked in `.claude/memory/INDEX.md`
  (Threads) and are **not** yet done; they are not a condition of this card.
